Falsifies `inter_process_communication::notification::verification::every_operation_preserves_the_invariant`.

The defect: the binding path replaces the waiter path instead of following it, so a signal with
the bound thread elsewhere counts its bits even though a thread is queued in `WAIT`. It is the
shape a reader writing "bound, else count" from §101 (notification objects)'s rules 2 and 3 produces if rule 1 is
forgotten.

Expected to fail: `assert!(n.invariant_holds())` when a waiter is seeded and the signal is not
bound-receiving: the word becomes non-zero with the waiter still queued, which is a thread asleep
beside a doorbell that has already rung.

